<!--
  ats_invalid_codigo_operativo.xml — codigoOperativo is not "IVA".

  Rule exercised: codigoOperativoType, ats.xsd:1476-1481. Its only enumeration
  facet is value="IVA" at ats.xsd:1478, and length 3 at ats.xsd:1479. "ATS" has
  the right length but is not in the enumeration, so the document is rejected.

  Element under test: iva/codigoOperativo, ats.xsd:608-610.

  Note the contrast with §3 of the feature doc: ats.xsd declares only eight
  enumeration facets in the entire schema and none of them is a VAT rate, a
  withholding concept or a document type. codigoOperativo and TipoIDInformante
  are the two values the schema really does pin down, and they are the only two
  literals the ATS v1 builder is allowed to hardcode.
-->
